{
  "case_id": "2006-05-493",
  "document_hash": "359c1a228a56a793fcb9adac51b014dfecbc660d2c9b9f37e20fa1cde17d08f1",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2006-05-493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "359c1a228a56a793fcb9adac51b014dfecbc660d2c9b9f37e20fa1cde17d08f1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-359c1a228a56-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This case concerns the constitutional sufficiency of California's catchall factor (k) instruction, which was given in the penalty-phase portion of California capital cases, and which directed the jurors to consider any other circumstance that extenuates the gravity of the crime, even though it is not a legal excuse for the crime."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice STEVENS",
      "case_id": "2006-05-493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "359c1a228a56a793fcb9adac51b014dfecbc660d2c9b9f37e20fa1cde17d08f1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-359c1a228a56-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Johnson, would you comment on the footnote on the -- on the -- drawing the distinction with regard to the dance contest that the defendant won in that case, between -- it's over here; I'm asking the question -- between facts that occurred before the crime and facts that might have occurred after."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KENNEDY",
      "case_id": "2006-05-493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "359c1a228a56a793fcb9adac51b014dfecbc660d2c9b9f37e20fa1cde17d08f1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-359c1a228a56-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How does post-crime prison conduct reduce the seriousness of a previous crime?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2006-05-493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "359c1a228a56a793fcb9adac51b014dfecbc660d2c9b9f37e20fa1cde17d08f1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-359c1a228a56-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In California, jurors are well aware what their task is at a sentencing determination. In California, the guilt and the death eligibility determinations are made during the guilt-phase trial and the jurors are expressly told, during the penalty-phase trial, that their lone determination, their one concern, is to decide between a sentence of death or a sentence of life without the possibility of parole."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2006-05-493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "359c1a228a56a793fcb9adac51b014dfecbc660d2c9b9f37e20fa1cde17d08f1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-359c1a228a56-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It would have -- well, it would foreclose consideration of all present good-character evidence, I believe. It would -- it would have foreclosed the consideration of Boyde's evidence, of Payton's evidence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2006-05-493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "359c1a228a56a793fcb9adac51b014dfecbc660d2c9b9f37e20fa1cde17d08f1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-359c1a228a56-0000-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The factor (k), as the entire standard instruction given in these cases, recites verbatim the language of the California statute, which is California penal code section 190.3."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-05-493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "359c1a228a56a793fcb9adac51b014dfecbc660d2c9b9f37e20fa1cde17d08f1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-359c1a228a56-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: So, the prosecutor, I take it, would have answered Justice Stevens's question the other way."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2006-05-493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "359c1a228a56a793fcb9adac51b014dfecbc660d2c9b9f37e20fa1cde17d08f1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-359c1a228a56-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Mr. Johnson, when I asked you about the derivation of factor (k), you gave me a California statutory cite, but is there -- does it come from any model code? Does any other State have such a provision? How widespread is it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2006-05-493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "359c1a228a56a793fcb9adac51b014dfecbc660d2c9b9f37e20fa1cde17d08f1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-359c1a228a56-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: How many States have an instruction that talks about extenuating the circumstances of the crime?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2006-05-493",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "359c1a228a56a793fcb9adac51b014dfecbc660d2c9b9f37e20fa1cde17d08f1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-359c1a228a56-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Mr. Multhaup, one aspect of your argument I wish you would clarify, and that's in your brief at page 20, footnote 3. As I understand it, you are saying -- you are not challenging factor -- the factor (k) instruction as excluding Skipper evidence. Your challenge is limited to this particular case. Is that what you're saying in that footnote?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-05-493",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "359c1a228a56a793fcb9adac51b014dfecbc660d2c9b9f37e20fa1cde17d08f1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-359c1a228a56-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: But we have said that remorse extenuates the gravity of the crime, for punishment purposes, under factor (k)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-05-493",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "359c1a228a56a793fcb9adac51b014dfecbc660d2c9b9f37e20fa1cde17d08f1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-359c1a228a56-0002-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted. [Whereupon, at 12:03 p.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.]"
    },
